I had to modify my Moodle 1.7 download to support the customization of the login panel (./login/index_form.html) for a special need.
I did it also for the signup panel and plan to do it for the forgot_password panel.

I think it could useful for other Moodle users and may help to add it to the standard Moodle theme features if you need.

How I did it (by the way Moodle code is very well organized) :

first I changed ./lib/weblib.php theme_setup function to calculate $CFG->login_panel et $CFG->signup_panel:
-----
/// Header and footer paths
    $CFG->header = $CFG->themedir .'/'. $theme .'/header.html';
    $CFG->footer = $CFG->themedir .'/'. $theme .'/footer.html';
    if (file_exists($CFG->themedir .'/'. $theme .'/login.html')) {
    	$CFG->login_panel = $CFG->themedir .'/'. $theme .'/login.html';
    } else {
    	$CFG->login_panel = $CFG->wwwroot .'/login/index_form.html';
    }
    if (file_exists($CFG->themedir .'/'. $theme .'/signup.html')) {
    	$CFG->signup_panel = $CFG->themedir .'/'. $theme .'/signup.html';
    } else {
    	$CFG->signup_panel = $CFG->wwwroot .'/login/signup_form.html';
    }
-----
then I changed ./login/index.php :
include("index_form.html"); 
became
include($CFG->login_panel);

and ./login/ signup.php :
include("signup _form.html"); 
became
include($CFG->signup_panel);

So simple and clean to do, thanks to your clever code.

hoping to be useful

