Description:
The course view page queries every course/module to see if you have manage (=delete) access so that if you do you get the 'turn editing on' button. For example if you have 50 course-modules this will cause 150 queries (coursemodules once each, contexts twice each).

Note that this does not apply to admin (or probably editing teacher), if you are admin it doesn't bother checking. Only for students.

I wrote a hack that does this by requesting the stuff at beginning and adding to various cache variables. It's a hack because it only works if you have internal memory cache on, etc.

In course/view just before the require_once for calendar/lib.php:

// ou-specific begins
    precharge_record_cache($course->id);
// ou-specific ends

In dmllib:

// ou-specific begins
/**
 * This function puts stuff in the record cache that is going to be needed to show a
 * course page in nearly all circumstances. It has the effect of reducing many (sometimes
 * hundreds) of individual queries into two bulk queries. There is also a genuine saving
 * of 1/3 of data transfer for this because the context stuff was requested twice.
 * @param int $courseid Course ID
 */
function precharge_record_cache($courseid) {
    global $CFG;    
    if(empty($CFG->rcache) || $CFG->rcache !== true) {
        // No point storing things if record cache is turned off
        return false;
    }
    // All the course modules are requested
    $records=get_records('course_modules','course',$courseid);
    if($records) {
        foreach($records as $record) {
            rcache_set('course_modules', $record->id, $record);
        }
    }
    // All the contexts are requested twice, once by ID and once by
    // contextlevel/instanceid
    $records=get_records_sql("
SELECT c.* 
FROM {$CFG->prefix}course_modules cm
INNER JOIN {$CFG->prefix}context c ON cm.id=c.instanceid AND c.contextlevel=70
WHERE
cm.course=$courseid 
");
    global $CONTEXT_PRECACHE;
    if($records) {
        foreach($records as $record) {
            rcache_set('context', $record->id, $record);
            $CONTEXT_PRECACHE[$record->contextlevel.'/'.$record->instanceid]=$record;
        }
    }
}
// ou-specific ends

get_record, after existing internal cache check:

// ou-specific begins    
    // Added to support special context cache - see precharge_record_cache
    if($table==='context' && $field1==='contextlevel' && $field2==='instanceid' && $field3==='' && $fields==='*') {
        global $CONTEXT_PRECACHE;
        if(isset($CONTEXT_PRECACHE) && array_key_exists($value1.'/'.$value2,$CONTEXT_PRECACHE)) {
            return $CONTEXT_PRECACHE[$value1.'/'.$value2];
        }
    }
// ou-specific ends

