This is not very straightforward. "Mentor/Parent" is a +role+ that is assigned in a context of a user. There can be multiple roles assignable in user context with different set of +capabilities+. For individual +capabilities+ we can backtrace who has given capability in the given [user] context. This may be required, for example, in the situation when we need to notify a parent that they need to agree to the child's privacy policy. We can also display list of such users (basically tell a child who are his parents) but only if we talk about specific action which is specific capability, speaking in moodle terms.

However in the general case we can not find users who are mentors/parents of the given user. And I would doubt that we should. Maybe individual student's behavior is monitored by a school psychologist or a different use case when the role setup was not designed to be transparent.

