Description:
At Seattle Academy, we have modifed the imap authentication method to first check the cached password before checking the external system.  It was suggested at the Hackfest that this should be the common strategy for most authenticiation methods.

Only if the person tries a password that does not match the cached password does it  check the external system.  This has the benefits:

1.  Moodle still operates when the external system is down.
2.  It speeds up all logins if there is latency in in the external system.

If a password is changed on the external system, once the user has used the new password, the cached password has changed.  Before that, either password will work.

Something like (I am not on my server, so it is probably a bit different).

if ($user = get_record('user', 'username', $username)) {
            if  ($user->password == md5($password)) {
                $this->return = true;
                return true;
            }
        }
        return false;

If this is implemented, some may want to require a check with the external system.  We don't.

S

