Description:
A large backup zip file should be made by backup task in a course which has a lot of files or large files(eg. *.mpg).
Pclzip library cannot make a large zip file over 2.0GB, 
on the other hand we can get a such large zip file by using external zip program.
But, PHP cannot copy a large file over 2.0GB.
We need long time for copying the file even if file size is smaller than 2.0GB.

We propose that using rename() instead of copy() in function copy_zip_to_course_dir(),
since we need to move only one zip file from temporary folder(moodledata/temp/backup/uniqueid) to
course folder (courseid/backup).
We do not need to use backup_copy_file().

Patch made by me is as follows;
--------------------

backup/backuplib.php, function copy_zip_to_course_dir()

        //Copy zip file
        if ($status) {
//          $status = backup_copy_file ($from_zip_file,$to_zip_file);
// Add from here
            umask(0000);
            if (rename($from_zip_file,$to_zip_file)) {
                chmod($to_zip_file,$CFG->directorypermissions);
                $status = true;
            } else {
                $status = false;
            }
// Add to here
        }

        return $status;
    }

----------------------------
After applying this modification, my server can complete backup task including 20GB zip file. (is not 2.0GB!)
(Using external zip prgoram for creating backup zip file)

