Description:
I am working on CONTRIB-728 which currently is a patch. The includecode module should be treated like a text label when printing/displaying the section (i.e. print_section function). There is a section of code that begins:

            if ($mod->modname == "label") {

it would be good if we could set up an parameter for modules to make it label-like. This would allow the includecode patch to be a true plugin. I'm not sure the best place to put it. We could add it to the modules table or store it in the plugin database. I would probably opt for storing it in the plugin database. In any case, we could then apply new parameter to label and replace the code with something like:

if ($mod->label) {

So if that parameter were true and it were a label or label-like then it would be displayed as such. This would give third party writers the ability to treat their module like a label without modifying code. 

Thanks for considering this. Peace - Anthony

