18/Mar/16 9:12 PM;60ca243120d2dd0070c77e82;Hi Arian,
good work on this issue, it is a really tricky one. I'm going to comment first on the upgrade script.

1. This gradebook freezing is different from all previous ones because it only happens in the master. There is no need to set and check upgrade_roundedgradeitems setting 

2. Please prefix function names {{get_letters}} and {{standardise_score}} with upgrade_ to avoid name conflicts

3. Your fix version is sometimes 20160320 and sometimes 20160314 - be careful when doing find&replace

4. It might be better performance-wise if you check for existing gradebook freeze in upgrade_rounded_grade_items() in the very beginning of foreach so you can skip all further queries and calculations

5. I do not quite understand why did you make function get_letters recursive. It is never called without context from upgrade_rounded_grade_items() since course_context::instance never returns null (it fails with exception if context not found). But even if it had IGNORE_MISSING as argument, the letters list should be taken from systems settings and not from their default values.

6. I am also worried about performance of this get_letters stuff - there is no caching and if you have 1000 courses where neither of them overrides letters the upgrade script will perform 4000 queries: for each course it will be 1 query to get context, 1 query to get letters for the course context, 1 for category and 1 for system. In the end after these 4000 queries you will get 1000 identical lists of system letters. The least you can do is to join the query in upgrade_rounded_grade_items with context table and this way you will know context path for each course - this is all you need in get_letters. Maybe some performance tuning for get_letters as well.  
This will also save you from calling context_course::instance from upgrade script (possibility of exceptions or future API changes).

Actually, thinking more about it - would not it be faster to go opposite way? Find all contexts where the letters boundaries were overridden, intersect them with the list of courses and then check 

It looks like it's not even 4000 queries - you seem to run the same script for every grade item. SQL query needs to use aggregation, maybe you need two separate queries for two checks. In one case you need to find all items and in another all courses. It it helps, here is an example of query that finds if course has letter items but maybe it is not needed:
{{MAX(CASE WHEN gi.value='3' THEN 1 WHEN gi.value='31' THEN 1 WHEN gi.value='32' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS hasletteritems}} group by course

7. get_config() is slow, look at MDL-51584 for example, they suggest that change like that significantly increases performance. It looks like you call get_config very often for the same course 
