If the username changes in an auth plugin, but the idnumber remains constant, we can detect this and rename the user in Moodle rather than create a new (duplicate) user.

This code could be used in moodlelib.php's create_user_record() function (at 3348 in 1.1291):

    // Check if rename is necessary based on duplicate idnumbers
    if ($newuser->idnumber) {
        $duplicate = get_record('user', 'idnumber', $newuser->idnumber);
        if ($duplicate && $duplicate->username != $newuser->username) {
            $old_username = $duplicate->username;
            $duplicate->username = $newuser->username;
            if (update_record('user', $duplicate)) {
                return $duplicate;
            } else {
                error_log('Failed to update username for renamed user: '.$old_username.' -> '.$newuser->username.' ('.$newuser->idnumber.')');
                return false;
            }
        }
    }

