file_storage.php. Several functions use $file_record parameters for input but most do not support it.

$file_record is convenient format because you can pass it around as one thing. But there is no way to go from a file_record to an actual file - you need to split it out into separate things again. For example I have code like the following in several places:

    $fileinfo = oucontent_get_documentfile_info($oucontent, $path, $filename);
    $fs = get_file_storage();
    $file = $fs->get_file($fileinfo->contextid, $fileinfo->filearea, 
        $fileinfo->itemid, $fileinfo->filepath, $fileinfo->filename);

obviously this is a bit annoying - could we add functions that take $file_record for the two get methods (get_file and file_exists)?

I have attached a patch, but I have not been able to test this (my system is not exactly working at present). If possible, could you review and apply it? On the plus side nothing uses these new functions yet so it won't break anything...

