Description:
The change in file.php that was made to handle [MDL-14495] should consider whether the request for the file resource is internal (e.g. a link on a course page) or external, such as from a user clicking on a link in an e-mail generated as a result of forum subscription.

In most cases it wouldn't necessarily be a problem but consider the case where the Moodle site is configured to use the Shibboleth SSO as the primary authentication method (manual being used only for administrative access).

In our site, I have modified the auth/shibboleth/auth.php file so that when a user has clicked on a link for a course, or some element within a course, they are taken (redirected) to the Shibboleth IdP login screen, rather than the usual /login/index.php where they would have to click again on some button or link to get to the IdP.

This worked fine, except for links to individual file resources. The file.php unconditionally passes false for the $setwantsurltome argument of require_login().

Instead, it should determine if the HTTP_REFERER server variable happens to be the same as $CFG->wwwroot, and if it is not (external request), use true for the $setwantsurltome argument. 

Example (file.php, beginning at line 59):

    // security: login to course if necessary
    // Note: file.php always calls require_login() with $setwantsurltome=false
    //       in order to avoid messing redirects. MDL-14495
    $setwantsurltome = (get_referer() != $CFG->wwwroot);
    if ($args[0] == 'blog') {
        if (empty($CFG->bloglevel)) {
            error('Blogging is disabled!');
        } else if ($CFG->bloglevel < BLOG_GLOBAL_LEVEL) {
            require_login(0, true, null, $setwantsurltome);
        } else if ($CFG->forcelogin) {
            require_login(0, true, null, $setwantsurltome);
        }
    } else if ($course->id != SITEID) {
        require_login($course->id, true, null, $setwantsurltome);
    } else if ($CFG->forcelogin) {
        if (!empty($CFG->sitepolicy)
            and ($CFG->sitepolicy == $CFG->wwwroot.'/file.php'.$relativepath
                 or $CFG->sitepolicy == $CFG->wwwroot.'/file.php?file='.$relativepath)) {
            //do not require login for policy file
        } else {
            require_login(0, true, null, $setwantsurltome);
