The new database API allows named parameters to be substituted into a query, using the following syntax
{quote}
// New syntax: named params
global $DB;
$params = array('firstname' => 'Peter', 'lastname' => 'Cantrophus');
$where =  "WHERE firstname = :firstname AND lastname = :lastname";
$user = $DB->get_record_select('user', $where, $params);
{quote}
However, it doesn't allow the re-use of a named parameter within the query, which can be useful when using OR statements, for example
{quote}
$params = array('siteid' => SITEID, 'course' => "%$course%");
$where = 'id != :siteid AND (shortname LIKE :course OR fullname LIKE :course)';
$courses = $DB->get_records_select('course', $where, $params);
{quote}
throws the error 
{quote}Incorrect number of query parameters. Expected 3, got 2.{quote}
I can see why it throws the error, but unless there's a specific reason not to, it would be nice to be able to re-use named parameters in this way.

